From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:55:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: reset MT6878 DSI to command mode

U-Boot can hand the MT6878 DSI controller to Linux with video mode still
selected.  The mainline host then mistakes that stale mode for an active
video stream while the panel bridge sends its first initialization command.
It waits for VM_DONE from a pipeline that has not produced a frame and
times out before sending any DCS data.

Reset MT6878 to command mode during host power-on.  Panel initialization
can then use the normal CMD_DONE transfer path, while atomic enable selects
and starts the requested video mode afterward.

Keep the behavior opt-in because only the MT6878 bootloader handoff has
been validated.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
index b61c179..85bd2db 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
@@ -193,6 +193,7 @@ struct mtk_dsi_driver_data {
 	bool has_size_ctl;
 	bool cmdq_long_packet_ctl;
 	bool support_per_frame_lp;
+	bool force_cmd_mode_on_poweron;
 };
 
 struct mtk_dsi {
@@ -718,6 +719,9 @@ static int mtk_dsi_poweron(struct mtk_dsi *dsi)
 		       dsi->regs + dsi->driver_data->reg_shadow_dbg_off);
 
 	mtk_dsi_reset_engine(dsi);
+	if (dsi->driver_data->force_cmd_mode_on_poweron)
+		mtk_dsi_set_cmd_mode(dsi);
+
 	mtk_dsi_phy_timconfig(dsi);
 
 	mtk_dsi_ps_control(dsi, true);
@@ -1284,6 +1288,7 @@ static const struct mtk_dsi_driver_data mt6878_dsi_driver_data = {
 	.reg_shadow_dbg_off = 0xc00,
 	.has_shadow_ctl = true,
 	.has_size_ctl = true,
+	.force_cmd_mode_on_poweron = true,
 };
 
 static const struct mtk_dsi_driver_data mt8183_dsi_driver_data = {
